ce justify tempering the rating consensus slightly, but not enough to move this out of Likely R.", "watch": "If additional independent polls confirm the tight September margins, or Cassidy's refusal to endorse Letlow fractures Republican turnout, the race could tighten further.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Bill Cassidy (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Louisiana's open Senate seat sits in a state that leans Republican by about eleven points, and Julia Letlow enters as the clear favorite. She has raised over $6 million and drawn roughly $11 million each in outside support and opposition, while Democrat Jamie Davis has raised about $2 million. Expert raters across the board call the race Solid or Safe Republican, and prediction markets price a Democratic win at under ten percent.\n\nStill, the polling picture is thinner than the ratings suggest. Two September surveys, both from Democratic-leaning pollsters, showed Letlow ahead by only about four points, and headlines have emphasized the narrow margin. That justifies a somewhat closer expected margin than the rating consensus implies, though the fundamentals of the state still make a Republican win the strong expectation.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0491, "margin": -9.91}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0664, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0312, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0328, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0575, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0895, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0752, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0962, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1593, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0833, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0984, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1142, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0801, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p